[TEXT] ## Confirmed Root Cause Found

**Router6's RIP configuration:**
```
router rip
 network 10.0.0.0/8
exit
```

Only `10.0.0.0/8` is declared — this covers **only eth2** (10.50.1.0/24, the uplink to router3). Router6's **eth0** (172.18.50.0/24) and **eth1** (172.18.51.0/24) are NOT included in any RIP network statement. RIP never advertises these connected subnets to router3, and consequently router4 (the PC11-PC14 gateway) has zero route to 172.18.51.0/24.

